          %title MacNeille real numbers
          %h1#macneille_real_numbers MacNeille real numbers
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#definition"} Definition
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#with_closed_sets"} With closed sets
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#with_open_sets"} With open sets
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#comparing_definitions"} Comparing definitions
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_other_kinds_of_real_numbers"} Relation to other kinds of real numbers
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#completeness"} Completeness
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#strict_ordering"} Strict ordering
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The MacNeille real numbers are a version of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            defined by forming the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MacNeille+completion"} MacNeille completion
            of the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ±
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm\infty
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+mathematics"} classical mathematics
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            (and if we include
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ±
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \pm\infty
            it produces the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/extended+real+numbers"} extended real numbers
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/constructive+mathematics"} constructive mathematics
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            be the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
            with its usual
            = succeed "." do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Archimedean order
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Archimedean+order"} ?
          %p
            There are two obvious ways to define the MacNeille real numbers from
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℚ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dedekind+cut"} cuts
            (which matches the general theory of
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/MacNeille+completions"} MacNeille completions
          %p Outside of these definitions themselves, we will adopt the open definition, since it relates better to other kinds of real numbers.
          %h3#with_closed_sets With closed sets
          %p
            A pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            is called a
            %strong closed Dedekind–MacNeille cut
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            if:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+bounds"} upper bounds
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in U
              iff for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in L
              = succeed ";" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ≥
                      %mi r
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \geq r
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is the set of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+bounds"} lower bounds
              of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in L
              iff for all
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in U
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ≤
                      %mi s
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \leq s
          %p
            Given two such cuts, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L_1, U_1) \leq (L_2, U_2)
            to mean:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_1 \subseteq L_2
              ; and
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊇
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \supseteq U_2
              \.
          %p (Actually, either of these assertions alone implies the other.)
          %p
            Then the set of such cuts becomes a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattice"} complete lattice
            = succeed "." do
              %strong extended MacNeille real numbers
            %strong MacNeille real numbers
            are the sub-poset consisting of the pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            are both
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
          %h3#with_open_sets With open sets
          %p
            A pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/subsets"} subsets
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            is called an
            %strong open Dedekind–MacNeille cut
            in
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℚ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Q}
            if:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is an extended
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+real+number"} lower real number
              and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is an extended
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+real+number"} upper real number
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is an open down-set and
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is an open up-set.
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              is the interior of the complement of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s \in U
              iff there is an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\lt s
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi r
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi L
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\notin L
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
              is the interior of the complement of
              = succeed ":" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in L
              iff there is an
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\gt r
              with
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi s
                      %mo ∉
                      %mi U
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\notin U
          %p
            Given two such cuts, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L_1, U_1) \leq (L_2, U_2)
            to mean:
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_1 \subseteq L_2
              ; and
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊇
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \supseteq U_2
              \.
          %p (Actually, either of these assertions alone implies the other.)
          %p
            Then the set of such cuts becomes a
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/poset"} poset
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complete+lattice"} complete lattice
            = succeed "." do
              %strong extended MacNeille real numbers
            %strong MacNeille real numbers
            are the sub-poset consisting of the pairs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            are both
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+set"} inhabited
          %h3#comparing_definitions Comparing definitions
          %p The open and closed definitions above are equivalent, even in constructive mathematics.
          %p
            In one direction, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            is a closed extended MacNeille real number, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^o
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^o
            to be the interiors of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            respectively. Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^o
            is an extended lower real and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^o
            is an extended upper real. If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in U^o
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\lt s
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\in U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            is such that
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi r
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\lt r \lt s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∉
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\notin L
            (and hence
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∉
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\notin L^o
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in L
            we would have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi t
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\le t
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\lt s
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∉
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\notin L^o
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\gt r
            with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\in L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\in L
            we have
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\le r
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in U
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in U^o
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^o
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi o
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi o
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^o,U^o)
            is an open extended MacNeille real number, which is bounded if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            is.
          %p
            In the other direction, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            is an open extended MacNeille real number, define
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^c
            to be the set of lower bounds of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^c
            to be the set of upper bounds of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^c
            is a function of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            rather than
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in L^c
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in U^c
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\gt s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            such that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi t
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\lt t\lt r
            we would have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∉
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\notin U
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi t
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\notin L
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in L
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in L^c
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in U^c
            then
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\le s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L^c
            consists of lower bounds for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^c
            and vice versa. Conversely, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            is a lower bound of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^c
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in L^c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                  %mo ,
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^c,U^c)
            is a closed extended MacNeille real number, which is bounded if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            is.
          %p
            To show that these operations are inverses, suppose first
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            is a closed extended MacNeille real. Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi o
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^o)^c
            is the set of lower bounds of the interior of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is of course a lower bound for its interior, so
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi o
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\subseteq (L^o)^c
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            is a lower bound for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^o
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in L
            it suffices to show
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\le s
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in U
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\gt s
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in U^o
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi U
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U^o
            is open. Thus
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi o
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L= (L^o)^c
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi o
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = (U^o)^c
          %p
            On the other side, suppose
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            is an open extended MacNeille real. Then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L^c)^o
            is the interior of the set of lower bounds of
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            consists of lower bounds for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is open, we have
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ⊆
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi c
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi o
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L \subseteq (L^c)^o
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi o
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in (L^c)^o
            then there is an
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %msup
                    %mi L
                    %mi c
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in L^c
            with
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\lt s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t
            with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi t
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\lt t\lt s
            we have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi t
                  %mo ∉
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} t\notin U
            (since
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            is a lower bound for
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in L
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi L
                      %mi o
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L= (L^o)^c
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi U
                      %mi o
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi c
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U = (U^o)^c
          %p On the rest of this page, we will adopt the open definition, since it relates better to other kinds of real numbers.
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#relation_to_other_kinds_of_real_numbers Relation to other kinds of real numbers
          %p
            Any (extended)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/located+real+number"} located real number
            is an (extended) MacNeille real number. The locatedness condition says that if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi s
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\lt s
            then
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r\in L
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi U
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s\in U
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi r
                  %mo ∉
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⇒
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi s
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (r\notin L)\Rightarrow (s\in U)
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi s
                    %mo ∉
                    %mi U
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi L
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s\notin U)\Rightarrow (r\in L)
          %p
            Similarly, if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            is an (extended) MacNeille real number, then by definition
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is an (extended)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/lower+real+number"} lower real number
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an (extended)
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/upper+real+number"} upper real number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            in a MacNeille real are recoverable from each other, this gives two order-embeddings.
          %p
            If we define an
            %strong interval
            to be a pair
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,U)
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            is an extended lower real,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            is an extended upper real, and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi L
                    %mo ∩
                    %mi U
                    %mo =
                    %mi ∅
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L\cap U = \emptyset
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi L
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi L
                  %mo ,
                  %mi int
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi L
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L,int(\neg L))
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi U
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi int
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ¬
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                  %mi U
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (int(\neg U),U)
            — two kinds of “singleton” intervals. These are both order-embeddings, and in fact the lower reals are a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/coreflective+subcategory"} coreflective
            sub-poset and the upper reals are a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/reflective+subcategory"} reflective
            sub-poset. Thus we have an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/adjunction"} adjunction
            between extended lower reals and extended upper reals, and the extended MacNeille reals are the jointly fixed sub-poset. They are also the set-theoretic
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
            of the lower and upper reals inside the intervals.
          %h3#completeness Completeness
          %p
            Since the extended MacNeille reals are a reflective sub-poset of the extended lower reals and a coreflective sub-poset of the extended upper reals, they are closed in the former under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infima"} infima
            and in the latter under
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/suprema"} suprema
          %h3#strict_ordering Strict ordering
          %p
            Recall that the MacNeille reals are a poset in which
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi U
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L_1, U_1) \leq (L_2, U_2)
            iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msub
                    %mi L
                    %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_1 \subseteq L_2
            iff
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ⊇
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \supseteq U_2
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            may be called the
            %em weak ordering
            on MacNeille reals.
          %p
            There is also a
            %em strict (or strong) ordering
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            defined by
          %ul
            %li
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 2
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (L_1, U_1) \lt (L_2, U_2)
              iff
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1
              meets
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_2
              (meaning that the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/intersection"} intersection
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi U
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∩
                    %msub
                      %mi L
                      %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} U_1 \cap L_2
              is
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inhabited+subset"} inhabited
          %p
            That is,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y
            iff for some rational number
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi q
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi y
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt q \lt y
          %p
            This restricts to the usual strict order
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &lt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \lt
            on Dedekind reals. We also have for any rational number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt q
            by this new strict order iff
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt q
            in the previously known sense (that
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            belongs to the upper set of
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo &gt;
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \gt q
          %p
            For Dedekind reals, the strict ordering is often taken to be the more basic concept, as the weak ordering can be derived from it (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/negation"} negation
            of
            = succeed ")." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo &gt;
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gt
          %p
            They are not entirely unrelated, however; we do have
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt z
            whenever
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mi y
                  %mo ≤
                  %mi z
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \lt y \leq z
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi y
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi z
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \leq y \lt z
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ≤
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \leq
            and
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo &gt;
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \gt
            is the negation of the other, they are mutually exclusive, and it is impossible for both to be false. As such, the pair of relations
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo ≤
                  %mo ,
                  %mo &gt;
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ({\leq},{\gt})
            makes the MacNeille real numbers into a tight interpretation of the classical theory of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/total+orders"} total orders
            in the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/antithesis+interpretation"} antithesis interpretation
